checks_run.procedure:
Run my six prior-round probes (byte-identical copies of round-5/repro) and the new round-6 probe form-export-label.r6.test.ts in the disposable clone on a disposable PostgreSQL, then remove them.

The prior probes cover:
- the AUD write and ADM-only read sweep, generated from openapi.yaml and p5-operations.ts;
- Studio co-author review and contributor paths (0097);
- the intake foreign-transformation claim (0096 Rule A);
- the demo portfolio and key-deliverables guards.

The new probe covers:
- scope of the labelled export;
- the mth_app marker writes;
- an explicit production marker;
- formula neutralization after the label row;
- the format/Accept guard.

Targeted reading of the P5 diff e70ac02..ad52a56 on this candidate. Areas:
- export ownership, download, cancel and the store keys;
- formula injection in XLSX and CSV;
- the automation dry-run rollback and worker identity;
- the relay's handling of an unregistered event type;
- 0096 Rule A;
- 0094's one-off trigger disable;
- the demo seeding and dev-issuer guards;
- evidence register sql.raw.

Check the structure:
- migrations: added-only status, numbering and contiguity;
- the contract operation count;
- the module graph (reporting does not import workflows or admin; the worker does not import the API).

Scan the 188,233 lines added in e70ac02..ad52a56 (apps, packages, deploy, e2e, tests, scripts) for:
- secrets;
- eval, new Function, innerHTML or child_process;
- external hosts;
- raw SQL;
- float arithmetic in product source.

Check the declared environmental residuals on the offline and configuration surface:
- live registry and live CI;
- Keycloak and the demo IdP;
- AI and external notification adapters.
